        "id": 1083225
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-02-23T20:43:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e I don\u0027t know how that works from a security release perspective though.\n\nYeah that is my main concern as well.\n\n\u003e Customers finding out in a month that something changed will still be an escalation + panic to figure out what to do about all the changes that weren\u0027t submitted that they expected to be submitted.\n\nFair point. Ok then I am convinced throwing an error is indeed the better solution.\n\n@beckysiegel@google.com do you have any input?",
      "parentUuid": "8bf57ae6_06785655",
      "revId": "48c6e20e1f5be0ddb01e000380ec12244d1faa8f",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3020e032_97edd51d",
